Yes, in Java, a stream can be reused, but only if it's a type of stream that supports it (like List, Set, etc.).
Most streams, especially those created by methods like Files.lines() or Stream.of(), are one-time-use.
Once a terminal operation is invoked (like forEach(), collect(), etc.), the stream is consumed and cannot be reused.
  
List<String> data = List.of("apple", "banana", "cherry");

// Create a Supplier that generates the stream
Supplier<Stream<String>> streamSupplier = () -> data.stream();

// Use the stream multiple times
streamSupplier.get().forEach(System.out::println);
streamSupplier.get().filter(s -> s.startsWith("b")).forEach(System.out::println);  
  
